UNIT.learningOutcomes:
By the end of the sub-strand, the learner should be able to:
a) outline the characteristics of organisms in the divisions of Kingdom Plantae, including Bryophyta, Pteridophyta and Spermatophyta (sub-divisions and classes of Spermatophyta);
b) classify organisms into phyla and classes of Kingdom Animalia;
c) construct dichotomous keys to identify plants and animals;
d) relate viruses to their economic importance in health, agriculture and biotechnology;
e) appreciate the diversity of plants and animals in nature.
